{
  "title": "Thumb CMC Dislocation",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/hand/10119/thumb-cmc-dislocation",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Mar 18 2025",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Thumb CMC Dislocations are rare injuries that occur due to axial force on a flexed thumb.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is clinical and can be confirmed by orthogonal radiographs.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is closed reduction and immobilization with unstable injuries requiring surgical stabilization.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Incidence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "makes up <1% of hand injuries",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Anatomic location",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Mostly dorsal dislocations",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/10119/images/fig_a1.jpg",
                  "caption": "dorsal cmc disloc"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Volar dislocations are rare",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/10119/images/screen_shot_2016-05-01_at_12.03.21_pm.jpg",
                      "caption": "volar thumb CMC disloc"
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "mechanism",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "axial force on a flexed thumb (more common)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "dorsal force applied in 1st web space (e.g. handlebar driven into a motorcyclist’s thumb on impact) (less common)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "pathoanatomy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "dorsoradial ligament is torn",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "anterior oblique ligament is stripped/peeled off the 1st metacarpal base but remains continuous",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Anatomy",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Dorsal side ligaments are the primary stabilizers to dorsal/dorsoradial forces",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "16 total ligaments that stabilize the TMC joint",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "superficial anterior oblique",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "does NOT stabilize joint in flexion",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "does NOT prevent dorsal subluxation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "provides for laxity of TMCJ to allow pronation during opposition",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "forms “voluminous pouch” to accommodate metacarpal translation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "deep anterior oblique (beak) ligament",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "pivot for TMCJ for pronation of thumb",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**dorsoradial ligament**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "stabilizer (“check rein”) to radial subluxation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "becomes taut with radial/dorsoradial subluxation before other ligaments",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "if all other ligaments but this one are cut, CMC still remains reduced",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "lax in stage IV arthritis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "posterior oblique ligament",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "ulnar collateral ligament",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "intermetacarpal ligament",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "dorsal intermetacarpal",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "dorsal trapeziotrapeziod",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "volar trapeziotrapeziod",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "dorso trapezio-II metacarpal",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "volar trapezio-II metacarpal",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "trapezio-III metacarpal",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "transverse carpal ligament",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "trapeziocapitate",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "volar scaphotrapezial",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "radial scaphotrapezial",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "7 main stabilizers of TMCJ – SAOL, dAOL, DRL, POL, UCL, IML and DIML",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "9 stabilizers of trapezium – DTT, VTT, DT-II MC, VT-II MC, T-III MC, VST, RST, trapeziocapitate and transverse carpal",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "4 key ligamentous restraints of the thumb",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "anterior oblique ligament",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "remains attached to volar fragment in Bennett/Rolando fracture",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "posterior oblique ligament",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "intermetacarpal ligament",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "dorsoradial ligament",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "recent literature suggests the **dorsoradial ligament** is the **primary stabilizer** preventing dorsoradial subluxation of the thumb CMC joint",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "History",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "collide onto fixed object/axial force on a flexed thumb",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "dorsal force applied to 1st web space",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "e.g. handlebar driven into a motorcyclist’s thumb on impact)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "pain over thenar eminence",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "swelling, bruising over thenar eminence",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "unable to form a fist",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
